STEP 2 - the app builds the actor straight from those headers. auth.ts:52 `const actor = (await actorFromBearer(headers.authorization)) ?? actorFromHeaders(headers)`; with no Authorization header actorFromBearer returns null (auth.ts:32) and actorFromHeaders (auth.ts:19-27) reads `headers['x-forwarded-subject']`, `headers['x-forwarded-account']` and splits `headers['x-forwarded-roles']` into the role array. adminOps is mounted unconditionally on the root chain (index.ts:25) with prefix '/ops' (accounts.ts:105) and its only gate is `if (!hasRole(actor, 'ops-admin'))` (accounts.ts:108) - which the attacker's own `X-Forwarded-Roles: ops-admin` satisfies. rateLimit does not meter this path either: middleware.ts:18 returns early unless the path starts with '/v1' (prefix set at index.ts:13).

